# Recoder — Open Work (not-done only)

Backlog / reference. Tracks only what is NOT done. Shipped history lives in git + commit messages.
Source of truth order: plan.md (execution) → remaining.md (paid-user gate) → prd.md/product.md (product) → this file.

## Paid-user launch gate (blocks first paid users)

- GitHub repo connection → task↔branch mapping → PR artifact creation → review/check sync → issue/task linking, verified against the deployed PR-artifact flow.
- Real task timeline (task → artifact → PR → preview → approval) from shared run history, not demo/per-page state.
- Live edge/preview rollout: DNS, TLS, protected preview hosts, rate limits, WAF hooks, production verification (recoder-zvss).
- Hetzner deploy hygiene: resolve local↔prod git divergence so full deploys don't need scoped checkout/build handling (recoder-js56).
- Production traffic/abuse controls once real signals exist (recoder-a9rp, recoder-rbc2 mitigation half).

## Security / hardening

- [recoder-0zso] `/api/a2a/*` auth hardening. **Reassessed 2026-06-03:** the "most routes unauthenticated" claim was stale — 29/35 already use `authenticateRequest`. Closed the concrete gaps: `adapters/rest` + `adapters/git` (arbitrary REST/repo-path operations), `terminals` + `terminals/summary`, `bridge/agents`, and now the live-consumed `workspaces/*` + SSE-stream mounts are authenticated on the main server. The workspace slice also enforces owner scoping, and EventSource consumers use the `?token=`→Authorization promotion path so mission-control/handoff/multi-dispatch streams keep working. Bridge WS tokens are already verified (`authenticateWebSocket` → `verifySessionToken`, no anon bypass). **Still open under recoder-0zso:** broader surface review/closure beyond the live workspace/SSE slice; the `.well-known/agent.json` discovery endpoint stays public by spec.

## Agent platform — next

- Squad dispatch → coding-runtime execution: shipped incl. **session-on-demand** (opt-in `execute`+`projectId`) and **container-from-nothing** (opt-in `createSandbox`: `provisionDaytonaSandboxForProject()` creates a fresh sandbox when the project has none, then starts a session + runs — a focused headless version of the web-IDE creation path that deliberately does NOT refactor the proven route). Execution status is **truthful** — the response carries `execution { requested, started, reason }`; the UI shows a warning with the reason on skip/provisioning failure instead of fake success. UI: 'provision sandbox if missing' checkbox on squad detail + board dispatch. Still TODO — a richer agent↔project mapping (which project an agent should act on, rather than a manually entered id).
- Workflow StepMode: `parallel` + `conditional` (then/else sub-step branches) steps shipped; Step Runner now supports step **reordering** + visual `{{_lastOutput}}` data-flow connectors. Still TODO — a squad-step node in the heavyweight **Giselle** visual designer (internal-packages/workflow-designer-ui), which has its own node-type system (recoder-agency product; larger, separate effort).
- ~~Per-agent drill-down beyond skills (run history).~~ Shipped — 'Recent runs' section in the Team-page agent panel (`GET /api/a2a/agents/:agentId/assignments`). Presence is surfaced on squad cards, squad detail, the Team roster, and the cross-squad **task board** (`/squads/board`) — board + squad detail refresh live via the collab SSE stream. The marketplace `/agents` list is a separate template-identity space, not A2A runtime presence, so it's intentionally excluded.

## Capability layer — follow-ups

- Self-host on prod: bring up Qdrant + ziti (NOT Ollama/vLLM — 16GB/no-GPU box); set cloud LLM + Gemini keys per `docker-backend/.env.capabilities.recoder-server`.
- Stand up OpenZiti controller end-to-end + provision a runner (`scripts/provision-ziti-runner.sh`); needs CA trust (NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS).
- Free prod disk (94% used; 135GB is vcpeer — do not touch) before enabling capability backends.
- Mine remaining variant ideas as needed: open-agents (sandbox context), GitNexus (incremental graph), pal-mcp-server (parser pluggability).
